Fixed in `tokio-stream/src/stream_map.rs:686`:

```rust
fn size_hint(&self) -> (usize, Option<usize>) {
    let mut ret: (usize, Option<usize>) = (0, Some(0));

    for (_, stream) in &self.entries {
        let hint = stream.size_hint();

        ret.0 = ret.0.saturating_add(hint.0);

        match (ret.1, hint.1) {
            (Some(a), Some(b)) => ret.1 = a.checked_add(b),
            (Some(_), None) => ret.1 = None,
            _ => {}
        }
    }

    ret
}
```

- Lower bound uses `saturating_add`, so it caps at `usize::MAX` instead of panicking in debug (and instead of silently wrapping in release).
- Upper bound uses `checked_add`, so an overflowing sum degrades to `None` — "no known upper bound" — which is the correct `Stream` contract answer, since `Some(usize::MAX)` would be a false claim of a real bound.
- The explicit `(usize, Option<usize>)` annotation is needed; without it the literal `0` stays an ambiguous integer type and the methods won't resolve.

`size_hint_overflow` passes, as does the rest of the `tokio-stream` suite (28 tests in `stream_stream_map`, no failures anywhere).
